    <briefdescription>
<para>Describes a HyperBus device. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One entry per supported device, looked up at runtime from the manufacturer and device identifiers read out of the part - IR0 and IR1 for HyperRAM.</para><para>This holds ONLY what the device cannot report about itself:</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Geometry is absent. Density, row/column bits, array rows and the address limit are all decoded from IR0 by the accessors below. So one entry serves every density in a family.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Directly readable register fields are not duplicated.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>Adding a device is therefore data, not code: append an entry and everything else follows. </para>    </detaileddescription>
